  "key_findings": "K912 decomposes MF-GJR's overall QLIKE advantage (-5.63% vs GJR) across VIX regimes. Largest advantage in High (25-35) (delta QLIKE=+0.211706), smallest in Crisis (>35) (delta QLIKE=+0.006702). Rolling advantage correlates with VIX (r=0.359). Tau contribution to total variance: Low (<15)=66%, Medium (15-25)=71%, High (25-35)=51%, Crisis (>35)=82%. MF-GJR's multiplicative structure captures VIX-driven long-run dynamics that single-component GJR misses.",
  "findings_list": [
    "MF-GJR advantage is largest in High (25-35) regime (delta QLIKE=+0.211706)",
    "MF-GJR advantage is smallest in Crisis (>35) regime (delta QLIKE=+0.006702)",
    "Rolling advantage correlates with VIX (corr=0.3588)",
    "Tau contribution INCREASES with VIX: from 65.6% (Low VIX) to 82.2% (highest regime)"
  ],
